// The services this tool is willing to move off Automatic start.
//
// The bar for being on this list is that somebody can plausibly not need the service and that
// the docs page can say what stops working -- not that turning it off has been shown to buy
// frames. Most of these are rated Plausible for exactly that reason, and the pages say so. An
// entry that is honest about being unproven is more useful than one that has been left out,
// because leaving it out does not stop anyone doing it; it only stops them doing it somewhere
// that keeps a receipt.
//
// What is NOT here is anything on WindowsServices.Protected: audio, boot, sign-in, networking
// and the security stack. Those are refused at the SCM layer, and naming one here throws while
// the catalog is being built rather than on a user's machine.
//
// Every entry offers Manual rather than Disabled by default. Manual means a wrong guess on this
// list costs a slower first start; Disabled means it costs a failure somewhere else, with no
// mention of the service or of this program.
//
// Fields: id, service (the SCM name), title, summary, category, evidence, tags. Risk is
// Moderate unless an entry says otherwise. Adding one needs a docs page with the same id --
// CI enforces that.
[
  // ---- indexing and caching
  {
    "id": "services.search-indexer",
    "service": "WSearch",
    "title": "Stop the Windows Search indexer starting at boot",
    "summary": "Windows Search rebuilds its content index in the background, which is real disk and CPU work that arrives without warning. Start menu search keeps working; results for file contents get slower.",
    "category": "startup",
    "evidence": "Plausible",
    "tags": ["service", "indexing", "disk"]
  },
  {
    "id": "services.sysmain",
    "service": "SysMain",
    "title": "Stop SysMain (Superfetch) starting at boot",
    "summary": "SysMain preloads what it predicts you will run next. On a hard disk that was a real win; on an SSD the prediction is worth much less than it costs, though how much less is not something anyone has measured for games.",
    "category": "startup",
    "evidence": "Plausible",
    "tags": ["service", "prefetch", "memory", "widely-shared"]
  },
  // ---- telemetry and reporting
  {
    "id": "services.telemetry",
    "service": "DiagTrack",
    "title": "Stop the telemetry collector starting at boot",
